color-management-v1: allow extended target volumes

The parametric creator already accepts target volumes outside the primary
color volume. Allow compositors whose renderer supports that content to
advertise it. Aqueous's Vulkan linear texture path preserves extended values
through luminance scaling and the primary conversion matrix, without clipping
to the primary color volume.

Mesa's Wayland WSI requires this capability, in addition to extended-linear
transfer and sRGB primaries, to enumerate EXTENDED_SRGB_LINEAR. This is separate
from the predefined Windows-scRGB request and its fixed 80-nit mapping.
Based on kode54's draft in Seafoam-Labs/Aqueous#130.

--- a/types/wlr_color_management_v1.c
+++ b/types/wlr_color_management_v1.c
@@ -1162,7 +1162,6 @@
 	assert(!options->features.set_primaries);
 	assert(!options->features.set_tf_power);
 	assert(!options->features.set_luminances);
-	assert(!options->features.extended_target_volume);
 
 	struct wlr_color_manager_v1 *manager = calloc(1, sizeof(*manager));
 	if (manager == NULL) {
